s6-1-p44 : Block
s6-1-p44 = prose (cons "For a substitution `σ` satisfying the context and face conditions, substitution stability gives a reduction from `t[σ]` to `u[σ]` with the corresponding type. A runtime may therefore reuse the already performed reduction under that substitution. It must then resume evaluation if `u[σ]` contains newly exposed redexes. A cached weak-head result for `u` is not automatically a weak-head result for every substitution instance." nil)
